---
code: lint-tool-output-unparsable
when-fires: an external linter produced non-empty output that no tier of the adapter ladder recognized. lint/source_external.rs. `{tool}` is the tool, `{output}` its bytes flattened to one truncated line (PASSTHROUGH).
why: 27R §4 - upstream drift may cost precision, never a crash and never silence, so the raw bytes ship as one opaque finding rather than being dropped. World-as-payload: replay never runs a foreign tool.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
warning[lint-tool-output-unparsable]: sm unrecognized `checkbashisms` output
(raw): possible bashism in - line 4 (should be '.'):

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-tool-output-unparsable
{{tool}} = "checkbashisms"
